      {
        "annotation_id": "26c6e642fef9458ca3233bb53843cfa4_15",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "8. He further relied on the order passed by the High Court of Judicature a t Bombay, Bench Aurangabad passed in Criminal Case No.42/2019 in the matter of Ramesh Murlidhar Sharma vs.\nState of Maharashtra & Anr.\n9. Chapter X of Section 48 of "
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "be348cc65959496dbf1ac073d25ebe48_16",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "STA"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "A memorandum of appeal or revision petition against conviction, except in cases where the sentence has been suspended by the Court below, shall contain a declaration to the effect that the convicted person is in custody or has surrendered a"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "c85eaadadc0e4a629217c4efe30af319_17",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "STA"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Where the sentence has been so suspended, the factum of such suspension and its period shall be stated in the memorandum of appeal or revision petition, as also in the application under Section 389 of the Cr.P.C.\"\n"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "eba939064538475f83cffa63a4f21715_18",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "STA"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "A n application under Section 389 of Cr.P.C shall, as far as possible, be in Format No.11 and shall be accompanied by an affidavit of the appellant/applicant or some other person acquainted with the facts of the case.\"\n1"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "e4a5440688054229921971f2e6df97eb_19",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "0 . A s per the rules which are framed by Jharkhand High Court Rule 159, are also requires surrender of the accused before the court below."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "1ba7b50d62cc4e4e8e34a178f1d05164_20",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "11. Considering the aforesaid Rules, the Hon'ble Supreme Court in Vivek Rai (supra) in para 10 and 11 has held as under :-\n\"10."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "37db4ef12ed142d1b3ede7de9ab4ff5c_21",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Only further submission put forward is that inherent power of the Court to direct listing of the case by exempting the requirement of surrender has been taken away."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "6d3649eda76841fcad2f3fe299bce3d8_22",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "It is pointed out that even in Supreme Court Rules prohibition against listing without surrender is not applicable if the court otherwise directs."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "6a53e2d3f49e48dd97804f23830f9709_23",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\nSuch exception is not to be found in the impugned Rule.\n11."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "2bee924e5c0b42e685ade1d0decc8de8_24",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "It has not been disputed even by the learned counsel for the High Court that the Rule does not affect the inherent power of the High Court to exempt the requirement of surrender in exception situations."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "804e87d377b04238bff9a94c6e961b10_25",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "It cannot thus, be argued that prohibition against posting of a revision petition for admission applies even to a situation where on an application of the petitioner, on a case being made out, the Court, in exercise of Ashok Kumar vs The St"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "c3893ffdeb82439c92c96ced3bd1e2b6_26",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": ", considers it appropriate to grant exemption from surrender having regard to the nature and circumstances of a case."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "88825d95e1dd4078a86fc4ca19a5ab6c_27",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Thus, the exception as found in corresponding Supreme Court Rules that if the Court grants exemption from surrender and directs listing of a case, the Rule cannot stand in the way of the Court's exercise of such jurisdiction has to be assum"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "c0e1c03b299f49adb6b6d58e64c98c39_28",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "RATIO"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "As per the judgment passed by Hon'ble Apex Court in exercise of inherent powers of High Court,\nthe High Court can consider it appropriate to exempt the accused from surrendering before the Court below having regard to the nature and circums"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "fe258d6ad02148e6bac3d453011d572b_29",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "RATIO"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "13. The present case is related to the offence under Section 59 of Food Safety and Standard Act,\n2006 and the petitioner is suffering from disease, document of which are available on record hence it can be treated as an exceptional case, th"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "a7a125b67c514ff88e50f515b1832f39_30",
        "summary_section": "decision",
        "labels": [
          "RPC"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:decision",
          "forbidden_labels:RPC",
          "suspicious_label:rpc"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "14. Thus, in the facts and circumstances of the case, without expressing any opinion on merits of the case, the application I.A.Nos.8897/2024 and 8471/2024 stand allowed."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "7d0271b096064bc1a586a11fbdd352ae_31",
        "summary_section": "decision",
        "labels": [
          "RPC"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:decision",
          "forbidden_labels:RPC",
          "suspicious_label:rpc"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "It is directed that subject to furnishing personal bond of Rs.50,000/ - with one solvent surety in the like amount to the satisfaction of the trial court for his appearance before the Registry of this Court on 12.08.2024 and on all other su"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "5603198ab84f4cda8546757dc7a74608_32",
        "summary_section": "decision",
        "labels": [
          "RPC"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:decision",
          "forbidden_labels:RPC",
          "suspicious_label:rpc"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "A copy of this order be sent to the Court concerned for it's compliance."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "06eaf5fb3cb9468bbcf9d1aaf0986389_33",
        "summary_section": "decision",
        "labels": [
          "RPC"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:decision",
          "forbidden_labels:RPC",
          "suspicious_label:rpc"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\n17. Let record of the courts below be requisitioned."
      }
